pined:
So many seasons I had forgot my Springs;
My cheeks had pined and perished from their orbs,
And all the youth-blood in them had grown white

Adam, my brother,
I might have pined away;
I, but none other:

pinioned:
The legends of their centuried sleep;
Your birds of peace white-pinioned float
O'er ruined fort and storied plain,

